  "problem": "What is the complex conjugate of $z=-3+7i?$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\overset{\u2015}{z}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=-3+7i,$ the imaginary part is $7i.$ Flipping the sign, we get $-7i.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=-3-7i.$",
